+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4415 as an offline, no-leaderboard Agent2World-style adaptive repair loop over exactly `ar25`, `tn36`, and `lp85`, checkpointing in that order and targeting exactly the next level beyond the authoritative `levels_reproduced` value in `ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml`. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/ar25/`, `environment_files/tn36/`, and `environment_files/lp85/` are non-empty, that the executable-world-model harness and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce` import, that TRM training is stood down, and that no leaderboard submission is attempted; missing environments MUST record `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for that target while continuing the others. For every available target, the workflow SHALL generate adaptive behavior-aware tests from the target's still-failing rollout behavior rather than from a fixed named-register list, SHALL preserve per-round verifier accuracy and adaptive-test pass-rate, SHALL keep held-out mechanic checks and fresh-agent-state leakage controls separate from solve claims, SHALL write per-game adaptive-test artifacts under `results/arc_e3/<game>/adaptive_tests_4415.json`, and SHALL report any residual still-wrong behavior as the gap class instead of converting passing adaptive tests into a solve. A new level SHALL count only when it is beyond the prior best and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` or an injected equivalent returns `offline_reproduced=true`/`reproduced=true` for the target level.
